From ad450d59a6505c7e746149240504a6db88b2f8a4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reixo <125610085+Reixo0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:26:50 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 13/19] arm64: dts: qcom: kaanapali-nubia-nx809j: Enable GPU

Point the zap shader at the device's signed one. The GMU and SQE firmware
are the generic linux-firmware ones.

On this board the GPU only initialises if the GMU isn't sent the CLX
(current limiting) table and the limits table that builds on it: with the
reference board's values its GMU never answers the first GX power vote.
Until the board's own values are known, boot with msm.hfi_skip=3.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-nubia-nx809j.dts | 7 +------
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-nubia-nx809j.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-nubia-nx809j.dts
index cb66254b6..b215edfe3 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-nubia-nx809j.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/kaanapali-nubia-nx809j.dts
@@ -799,12 +799,7 @@ &adspslpi_mem {
 };
 
 &gpu {
-	/*
-	 * Enabled by default in kaanapali.dtsi. Keep it off until the GPU
-	 * clocks and zap shader are sorted out: MSM DRM binds the GPU as part
-	 * of the display, so a failing GPU takes the display down with it.
-	 */
-	status = "disabled";
+	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &gpu_zap_shader {
-- 
